Body:
hi, I also met this problem with OpenCode 1.17.13. I have setup this in `~/.config/opencode/opencode.json`, but nothing works.
```
{
    "tui": {
        "mouse": false,
        "auto_scroll": false
    }
}

```

Confirming this is still broken in v2.1.0 (released 2026-07-04). The createPhaseReminderHook in dist/index.js is byte-for-byte identical to v1.1.2 for the mutation step:

lastUserMessage.parts.push({
  type: "text",
  text: PHASE_REMINDER,
});

No PR referenced in either v2.0.x or v2.1.0 release notes touches this hook. The <internal_reminder> block still appears at the end of every orchestrator user message in the UI and chat history.

Any chance this can be prioritized? The suggested fix (inject via system prompt instead of a user message part) is a small, self-contained change that would fully close this issue without needing any changes on the OpenCode side.

Happy to open a PR if it would help.
